 "note": "The files of the upstream tree that the eight DFL baselines load on the three problems. upstream_sha256 is the sha256 of the file at the commit. An edited file carries a comment line that says so and has its own sha256. The origins of parts of the upstream code are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.",
 "settings": [
  "Batch size 1 for every method. The upstream benchmark scripts (shells/benchmarks/budget.sh, knapsack-energy.sh and bimatching.sh) use the default 256 for Blackbox and Identity, and for SPO on BA and KP.",
  "One hidden layer of 8 or 12 tanh units. The upstream defaults are 32 ReLU units.",
  "Early stopping with patience 50. The upstream default is 40.",
  "LODL uses openpto/config/models/lodl/lodl5k.yaml (5000 samples, sum reduction) on all three problems. The upstream KP script uses default.yaml (500 samples, mean reduction); the upstream BA script names a lodl5k.yaml path that does not exist at the commit.",
  "The Adam learning rate 0.01 and one optimizer step per epoch are the upstream defaults; the 300 epochs are those of the upstream benchmark scripts.",
  "The problem classes are replaced by those of baselines/dfl_problems.py: the data of this repository, a linear BA objective with an argmax decision and a linear predictor output (upstream: ReLU), and exact BM assignments on VALID and TEST.",
  "baselines/dfl.py redirects the two random.seed calls of the LODL code to the model seed."
 ],
