   "changes": [
    "The import of openpto.problems.RMAB, a module that upstream does not contain at this commit, and the branch that uses it are removed. Without this the file cannot be imported.",
    "A sampled decision is scored under the true coefficients of its instance. Upstream takes the objective that get_decision returns, which is computed under the sampled coefficients.",
    "The surrogate loss is fitted to the sampled regrets by the sum of squared errors. Upstream uses the two-stage loss of the problem, which is the binary cross-entropy for BM and the same sum of squared errors for BA and KP.",
    "The centre Y of the surrogate WeightedMSE, the one used here, is a buffer. Upstream makes it a trainable parameter, so it moves while the surrogate is fitted."
   ],
